ZOOM_EX_PANEL_METERS=Panel meters
ZOOM_EX_LCD_BY_HAND=Character LCD by hand
ZOOM_EX_SCOPE_RC=RC on an oscilloscope
ZOOM_EX_COUPLER_CURVE=Path of a linkage
ZOOM_EX_LIGHT_TEMP=Night light and thermometer
ZOOM_EX_BY_HAND=By hand
ZOOM_EXW_TURN_CRANK=Turn the crank: drag round it
ZOOM_EXW_DRAG_WEIGHT=Drag the weight
ZOOM_EX_SOLENOID=Solenoid and flyback diode
ZOOM_EX_STEPPER=Stepper motor
ZOOM_EX_SHAFT_SENSORS=Shaft sensors
ZOOM_EX_BELTS=Belts and chains
ZOOM_EX_CAM=Cam and follower
ZOOM_EX_RATCHET=Ratchet and pawl
ZOOM_EX_DAMPER=Damper
ZOOM_EX_WORM=Worm gear
ZOOM_EX_DECADE=Decade counter
ZOOM_EX_FLIPFLOPS=Flip-flops: SR and JK
ZOOM_EX_COMPARATOR=Comparator night light
ZOOM_EX_THYRISTORS=SCR and TRIAC
ZOOM_EX_POWER_SUPPLY=Power supply
ZOOM_EX_LIGHT_LINK=Light: optocoupler and sensors
ZOOM_EX_SPEAKER_TONE=Speaker tone
ZOOM_EXW_FLIPFLOPS=Tap S and R to set and reset the latch; with J and K at 1 the flip-flop changes on each tick
ZOOM_EXW_COMPARATOR=Turn the light down with its slider and the LED comes on; tap the pot to change the threshold
ZOOM_EXW_THYRISTORS=Tap G to fire the SCR (it stays on), its switch to stop it; close the TRIAC’s switch
ZOOM_EXW_SCOPE=Tap the knobs while it plays: a knob’s right side makes the wave bigger (or moves it up), its left side smaller
ZOOM_EX_TRAFFIC=Traffic lights at a crossroads
ZOOM_EX_PIANO=A 555 piano
ZOOM_EX_STRANDBEEST=Strandbeest legs (Jansen linkage)
ZOOM_EX_ENGINE=Four-stroke engine
ZOOM_EX_SOLENOID_ENGINE=Solenoid engine
ZOOM_EXW_TRAFFIC=A 555 steps the CD4017 once a beat; each of its outputs lights, through its diodes, the lights of that step and its number in binary. Tap INH to hold it, RST to start again
ZOOM_EXW_PIANO=Press and hold the keys while it plays; tap the volume knob to change it; the oscilloscope shows each note
ZOOM_EXW_STRANDBEEST=Theo Jansen’s leg: eleven bars on one crank. Each foot moves level along the ground, then lifts and comes back: it walks
ZOOM_EXW_ENGINE=A starter turns the crank: the piston goes down (intake: the left valve opens), up (compression), down (power), up (exhaust: the right valve opens). The timing belts turn the camshafts at half speed
ZOOM_EXW_SOLENOID_ENGINE=It starts by itself: the cam blocks the slotted sensor for half of each turn, firing the coil, which pulls the crank round. The switch stops it
ZOOM_EXW_LIGHT=Change the light with the sliders while it plays; tap the switch to light the optocoupler’s LED
ZOOM_EXW_RATCHET_DRAG=Drag the wheels round: the one with a pawl turns one way only
ZOOM_EXW_NO_DIODE=No diode: hold its button, then let go
ZOOM_EXW_SLIDERS=Change the light and the temperature with the sliders while it plays, or tap the sensors
ZOOM_EXW_LCD_STEPS=1. Press the E button (on the left): with D0–D3 on, as they start, the display turns on (a blinking cursor). 2. Turn RS on, and only D3 and D6 on: press E, an H. Each press of E writes what is set.
ZOOM_EXW_TAP_SHORT=Tap the switch: a short
ZOOM_EXW_NO_FUSE=No fuse
ZOOM_EXW_BACKWARDS=backwards
ZOOM_EXW_RESTART=Restart: new parts
ZOOM_EX_SERVO_TESTER=Servo tester
ZOOM_EX_WORKBENCH=Workbench
ZOOM_EX_EVERYTHING=Everything at once
ZOOM_LIB_CUSTOM=Custom
ZOOM_CUSTOM_EMPTY=Nothing kept yet: lasso something and press Keep, or Make part. Hold one here to edit, rename or delete it
ZOOM_CUSTOM_EDIT=Edit
ZOOM_CUSTOM_INSIDE=Inside
ZOOM_CUSTOM_RENAME=Rename
ZOOM_CUSTOM_DELETE_SURE=Delete “{0}”?
ZOOM_CUSTOM_DELETED=“{0}” deleted
ZOOM_CUSTOM_RENAMED=Renamed “{0}”
ZOOM_CUSTOM_NAME=Its name
ZOOM_TEMPLATE_EDITING_PART=Inside “{0}”: what you change here, every one of it on every canvas does; Back returns
ZOOM_TEMPLATE_EDITING_PIECE=Editing “{0}”: what is here is kept as it, from now on; Back returns
ZOOM_TEMPLATE_PART_UPDATED=“{0}” updated everywhere: {1} inputs, {2} outputs
ZOOM_TEMPLATE_PIECE_UPDATED=“{0}” kept as it is now
ZOOM_TEMPLATE_NOT_UPDATED=“{0}” not updated: it needs logic inputs and probes, and parts between them
ZOOM_DISPLAY=DISPLAY
ZOOM_SHOW_FPS=Frames per second, top right
ZOOM_OFF=Off
ZOOM_ON=On

